<section>
    <h2 class="mobile-centred-heading">Linkstyle Usage</h2>
    <p>
        The following examples use the same set as styles as the buttons, in this instance they are applied to an anchor (link) element, with the <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">Button.LinkStyle</span> modifier added.
        <b>Note: </b>All of the CSS classes have variables for both light and dark schemes. Click the Theme button at the top of the page
        to switch between light and dark modes.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Note: </strong> all of the links have a <span class="@CodeSpan.Base">href</span> pointing to the home page. Use your mouse
        to hover over the link to see the background change, or just tab to see both the background change and focus indicator.
    </p>
    <p>
        The following shows an example styling the element to be a regular size without any scheme so the default styles are applied.
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CssClassesSnippets.Button_Regular_Default_Example" AriaLabel="Link button styling code example" />
    <p>
        <a href="/" class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.Regular) @Button.LinkStyle">Settings</a>
    </p>

    <h3>Default component styling</h3>
    
    <p>All of the links have a transparent background until hovered or focused.</p>

    <div class="@FlexContent.Base @FlexContent.Wrap(UnitFlexWrap.Wrap) @Gap.SetGaps(UnitGapSize.Five) @Margin.Block(UnitSpace.Five)">
        <a href="/" type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.Size(ButtonSize.Small) @Button.LinkStyle">Default Small</a>
        <a href="/" type="button" class="@Button.Base @Button.LinkStyle">Default Regular</a>
